WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.634 --> 00:00:06.575
What is the world's most popular drink?

2
00:00:07.256 --> 00:00:11.358
What drink has played an important role in the world's history, politics, and religion?

3
00:00:12.038 --> 00:00:14.139
What drink is over five thousand years old?

4
00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:21.363
The answer is tea, and its story begins with Chinese Emperor Shen Nung, a scholar and scientist who

5
00:00:21.403 --> 00:00:23.224
lived over five thousand years ago.

6
00:00:23.965 --> 00:00:29.248
The emperor had ruled that throughout his kingdom all drinking water must be boiled as a hygienic precaution.

7
00:00:30.136 --> 00:00:35.078
One day while visiting a distant region, the emperor stopped to rest, and the servants began to boil

8
00:00:35.138 --> 00:00:36.398
water for everyone to drink.

9
00:00:37.218 --> 00:00:41.960
At this moment, the wind blew and some dried leaves from a nearby bush fell into the boiling

10
00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:44.140
water. The liquid became brown.

11
00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:50.402
As a scientist, the emperor was interested in the new liquid, drank some, and found it very refreshing.

12
00:00:51.062 --> 00:00:52.883
The tree was a wild tea tree.

13
00:00:53.583 --> 00:00:56.424
And so, according to legend, tea was created.

14
00:00:57.260 --> 00:01:00.582
From ancient times tea was renowned as a healthy, refreshing drink.

15
00:01:01.303 --> 00:01:05.046
The first detailed description of tea was written in 350 AD.

16
00:01:05.806 --> 00:01:09.108
Fresh, green tea leaves were picked, then pressed into hard "bricks."

17
00:01:09.849 --> 00:01:14.953
These bricks were roasted, crumbled into water, and boiled with onion, ginger, and orange.

18
00:01:15.733 --> 00:01:20.857
It was not until the Tang Dynasty that tea became China's national drink and the word "cha" was

19
00:01:21.037 --> 00:01:22.198
used to describe tea.

20
00:01:22.858 --> 00:01:28.229
The first book on tea, called Cha Ching, was written by Lu Yu in 780 AD.

21
00:01:29.010 --> 00:01:33.451
It had three volumes and described tea cultivation and preparation in ancient China.

22
00:01:34.112 --> 00:01:40.494
The modern term "tea" derives from words such as tchai, cha, and tay in early Chinese dialects.

23
00:01:41.335 --> 00:01:43.736
Its botanical name is Camellia sinensis.

24
00:01:44.516 --> 00:01:47.998
Tea is an evergreen plant with smooth, shiny, pointed leaves.

25
00:01:49.058 --> 00:01:53.400
After China, the first two countries to adopt tea were its neighbors, Korea and Japan.

26
00:01:54.112 --> 00:02:00.616
Tea first came to Korea during the Unified Shilla Dynasty, between 57 BC and 935 AD.

27
00:02:01.336 --> 00:02:05.558
As it was in China, tea was used for social and religious purposes in Korea.

28
00:02:06.199 --> 00:02:11.341
Tea was drunk socially among the royal family and aristocrats, and Buddhist monks drank tea to help them

29
00:02:11.401 --> 00:02:12.822
stay awake during meditation.

30
00:02:13.483 --> 00:02:16.244
Tea drinking became widespread in the Goryo Dynasty.

31
00:02:16.864 --> 00:02:22.608
During this time, special ceramic cups and bowls for tea drinking were designed, and an elaborate tea ceremony

32
00:02:22.648 --> 00:02:23.228
was developed.

33
00:02:24.084 --> 00:02:28.945
The ceremony begins with pouring the boiling water into a bowl, where it stands until it cools to

34
00:02:28.985 --> 00:02:30.566
about 60 degrees Celsius.

35
00:02:31.326 --> 00:02:33.887
If the water is too hot, the tea will be too bitter.

36
00:02:34.567 --> 00:02:38.848
The teapot and cups are warmed with some of the water, and then the tea leaves are warmed

37
00:02:38.888 --> 00:02:39.588
in the teapot.

38
00:02:40.368 --> 00:02:44.149
Then, the water is poured into the teapot and left to brew for two or three minutes.

39
00:02:44.950 --> 00:02:49.031
When the tea is poured, each cup is filled little by little so that the taste is evenly

40
00:02:49.071 --> 00:02:50.451
distributed in all the cups.

41
00:02:51.231 --> 00:02:56.029
The tea must be sipped slowly, and as you sip, you must think about the four characteristics of

42
00:02:56.109 --> 00:03:01.993
tea according to Korean Buddhism: peacefulness, respectfulness, purity, and quietness.

43
00:03:02.773 --> 00:03:09.697
During the Joseon Dynasty, Confucianism replaced Buddhism as the court religion, and wine replaced tea as the favored

44
00:03:09.717 --> 00:03:14.280
drink. Tea went out of fashion and was not revived until five hundred years later.

45
00:03:15.220 --> 00:03:21.244
Tea was introduced to Japan in 1191 by Yeisei, "The Father of Tea," a traveling Buddhist monk.

46
00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:26.903
As in Korea, tea was first used by Buddhist monks and aristocrats, and then spread to the rest

47
00:03:26.923 --> 00:03:27.583
of society.

48
00:03:28.244 --> 00:03:31.466
By this time, tea was no longer served in "cakes" but was powdered.

49
00:03:32.186 --> 00:03:35.388
Tea became so popular that even a tea guessing game was played.

50
00:03:36.088 --> 00:03:42.112
Beginning in early morning and continuing well into evening, guests would sample as many as fifty varieties of

51
00:03:42.172 --> 00:03:44.473
tea, trying to guess their places of origin.

52
00:03:45.194 --> 00:03:49.116
From the fourteenth to sixteenth centuries, a Japanese tea ritual was developed.

53
00:03:49.792 --> 00:03:54.993
The Japanese tea ceremony takes place in a special room designed for tea drinking and consists of many

54
00:03:55.053 --> 00:03:57.314
small rituals that have to be learned by heart.

55
00:03:58.034 --> 00:04:02.876
It is much more elaborate than the Korean ceremony, and almost every hand movement is prescribed.

56
00:04:03.676 --> 00:04:06.076
Tea didn't reach Europe until the fifteenth century.

57
00:04:06.777 --> 00:04:10.998
As the Europeans increased their trade with China, rumors of a new substance circulated.

58
00:04:11.658 --> 00:04:14.779
When tea finally arrived, people were unsure how to use it.

59
00:04:15.559 --> 00:04:19.520
One writer suggested that tea leaves be boiled, salted, buttered, and eaten!

60
00:04:20.284 --> 00:04:24.166
Some doctors and scholars also warned that this strange dark liquid was unhealthy.

61
00:04:24.866 --> 00:04:28.308
In reality, tea drinking actually increased the health of people in Europe.

62
00:04:28.988 --> 00:04:33.750
Water was too dangerous to drink at the time, so people drank beer at breakfast, lunch, and dinner!

63
00:04:34.371 --> 00:04:39.353
Tea, made with boiled and therefore safe water, was a vast improvement in the European diet.

64
00:04:40.073 --> 00:04:45.096
Nowadays, black tea is Britain's national drink, but Britons were the last Europeans to adopt it.

65
00:04:45.804 --> 00:04:51.366
Within fifty years, however, tea became so popular in Britain that Britain was the largest tea importer in

66
00:04:51.466 --> 00:04:57.047
Europe. Over the next few centuries, tea played a major role in world history and politics.

67
00:04:57.927 --> 00:05:00.528
European companies bought tea from China and India.

68
00:05:01.188 --> 00:05:06.110
The East India Company, in fact, became so rich and powerful that it ruled the nation of India

69
00:05:06.170 --> 00:05:07.110
for several years.

70
00:05:07.830 --> 00:05:13.252
This British company forced Indian workers to produce the drug opium, which was sold to China in exchange

71
00:05:13.292 --> 00:05:13.692
for tea.

72
00:05:14.400 --> 00:05:20.143
In the 1800s, England was the largest drug trafficking organization in the world, and was responsible for a

73
00:05:20.203 --> 00:05:24.505
devastating drug addiction problem in China—all just to control the trade in tea.

74
00:05:25.186 --> 00:05:28.388
In the new colony of America, tea was also causing trouble.

75
00:05:29.088 --> 00:05:36.072
In 1773, in a famous incident called the Boston Tea Party, 340 chests of tea were emptied into

76
00:05:36.092 --> 00:05:36.512
the ocean.

77
00:05:37.320 --> 00:05:43.183
Residents of Boston were protesting against the same company, the East India Company, and their protest was one

78
00:05:43.223 --> 00:05:45.965
of the first incidents that led to the American Revolution.

79
00:05:46.825 --> 00:05:52.408
In the nineteenth century, tea led to the creation of two new meal times: "morning tea" and "afternoon

80
00:05:52.468 --> 00:05:57.411
tea." A woman who managed a bread shop in England convinced her bosses to allow her to serve

81
00:05:57.471 --> 00:05:59.092
tea to her favorite customers.

82
00:05:59.852 --> 00:06:04.475
The shop set up some tables in 1864 and a new form of socializing was born.

83
00:06:05.275 --> 00:06:10.802
As one famous author said, "For the English, afternoon tea is really a picnic indoors."

84
00:06:11.542 --> 00:06:15.845
Morning tea and afternoon tea are still common in Britain and Commonwealth countries.

85
00:06:16.725 --> 00:06:21.488
Iced green tea was served with alcohol in the United States in the 1800s, but it was not

86
00:06:21.528 --> 00:06:23.989
until 1904 that iced tea really took off.

87
00:06:24.789 --> 00:06:27.651
At the World's Fair, hot tea was given away free for guests.

88
00:06:28.451 --> 00:06:32.594
Because of the intense heat, ice was added to the tea and it became an instant hit!

89
00:06:33.354 --> 00:06:36.916
Today, iced tea is usually made with lemon and sweetened with sugar.

90
00:06:37.980 --> 00:06:41.601
Nowadays, tea comes in green, black, and oolong varieties.

91
00:06:42.441 --> 00:06:48.943
Europeans and Americans have traditionally favored black teas, Asians prefer green tea, and Indians and East Asians drink

92
00:06:48.963 --> 00:06:50.424
a spiced tea called chai.

93
00:06:51.044 --> 00:06:57.526
However, the health benefits of green tea, including reducing the risks of cancer, are increasing its popularity worldwide.

94
00:06:58.206 --> 00:07:03.908
Herbal "tea," sometimes called a tisane or an infusion, is made by infusing herbs other than the tea

95
00:07:03.968 --> 00:07:04.968
plant in hot water.

96
00:07:05.800 --> 00:07:08.642
Hundreds of different kinds of herbal tea are drunk around the world.

97
00:07:09.482 --> 00:07:13.865
Some of the most popular are chamomile, mint, rosehip, and ginger.

98
00:07:14.605 --> 00:07:20.128
Many blends of real tea are prepared by adding other plants; for example, the popular Earl Grey tea

99
00:07:20.248 --> 00:07:22.289
is black tea infused with bergamot.

100
00:07:23.230 --> 00:07:26.352
Tea has been a part of human culture since the earliest written records.

101
00:07:27.172 --> 00:07:31.595
It has shaped societies, started wars, and changed the course of history.

102
00:07:32.355 --> 00:07:33.736
All because of a simple drink!

103
00:07:34.452 --> 00:07:40.036
William Gladstone, the prime minister of England, summed it up nicely: "If you are cold, tea will warm

104
00:07:40.076 --> 00:07:45.399
you; if you are too heated; it will cool you; if you are depressed, it will cheer you;

105
00:07:45.919 --> 00:07:48.141
if you are exhausted, it will calm you."
